WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:01.928
- So, I have a Pomeranian.

00:00:01.928 --> 00:00:03.592
His name is Jax.

00:00:03.592 --> 00:00:08.055
14 years ago, I thought I was
going to lose him forever.

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:11.144
So, he was a puppy, I was a little kid,

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.712
and we were taking a road trip.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.248
My parents were driving.

00:00:14.248 --> 00:00:16.213
I was staying in the backseat.

00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:18.072
His head was out the window.

00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:19.704
The wind was blowing through his hair,

00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:23.871
and then suddenly, the wind
just carried him out the window.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.000
Oh my god, Jax!

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.520
I thought my dog was gone.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.752
And I don't know if you've ever,

00:00:29.752 --> 00:00:31.112
if you ever seen that movie White Chicks,

00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:32.968
it was pretty much like literally

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.532
like that scene in that movie.

00:00:34.532 --> 00:00:36.104
At this point, I'm crying.

00:00:36.104 --> 00:00:38.360
My mom is screaming.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.952
My dad's trying not to crash the car.

00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:43.048
But it turned out he
was still on his leash,

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:46.230
and I look outside, Jax is just loving it.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.477
I'm holding onto his leash,

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:49.813
and he's just smiling the whole time

00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:52.695
as the wind is blowing
against the side of the car.

00:00:52.695 --> 00:00:55.096
If I wasn't holding onto
him, he would've been gone.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:56.934
I managed to reel him back in.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.517
He made it back safely.

00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:01.848
He didn't even realize that
he was in so much danger.

00:01:01.848 --> 00:01:06.484
Even though he's a lot bigger
now, super protective of him.

00:01:06.484 --> 00:01:10.651
If your dog is one pound and
he's staring out the window,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.166
hold onto him, please.

00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:16.312
(giggles)

00:01:16.312 --> 00:01:19.062
(cheerful music)

00:01:39.016 --> 00:01:41.349
(swooshing)

